#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:5
#: 50d40d3c7b2742b5950994f669887529
msgid "Guided Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:7
#: db87c460073b4e889575eee0b7c86792
msgid "Guided mode is a capability of Copter to dynamically guide the copter to a target location wirelessly using a telemetry radio module and ground station application. This page provides instructions for using guided mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:12
#: 29baea3ff7c344fe85ea32ffcf9dbc96
msgid "Guided Mode can also be used by LUA scripts and companion computers to command vehicle movement and navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:15
#: fd50feaefb2149ca9cae878113459e76
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:17
#: b2dc66ac5b6a40eaa10109865945323f
msgid "Guided mode is not a traditional flight mode that would be assigned to a mode switch like other flight modes. The guided mode capability is enabled using a ground station application (such as Mission Planner) and a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>`. This capability allows the pilot to interactively command the copter to travel to a target location by clicking on a point on the Mission Planner Flight Data map. Once the location is reached, the copter will hover at that location, waiting for the next target. Follow Me mode also uses Guided Mode to make the copter follow the pilot around the field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:32
#: 39dbec93c6c64381bf7ad9c317a2936c
msgid "What you'll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:34
#: 15aa37d3aa6b48599eaf186226b53776
msgid "To use guided mode, you'll need a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>` allowing your computer and autopilot to communicate during flight, a ground station computer or tablet, and a ground station application such as :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:home>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:40
#: aa0b11807e7e4e75a28a9f56ce9c2335
msgid "Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:42
#: e11eb50209b44b87b5a09027e9505d8a
msgid "Set up your copter at the field and establish a MAVLink connection over wireless telemetry between your copter and your laptop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:44
#: e633a72f622e4314917a703c32e12fa3
msgid "On your laptop, using the software that came with the telemetry module, make sure that it's working and that you have a GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:46
#: 5f981f3671a94212a01037089c30802e
msgid "Take off in :ref:`Loiter Mode <loiter-mode>` and climb to a safe altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:47
#: 4dec95ee5af64ea29b45f7e4b248739b
msgid "In the Mission Planner Flight Data screen map, try right-clicking on a nearby spot and select \"Fly to Here\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:49
#: 245024db1cb14138a2564eab74c5289d
msgid "You will be asked for a guided mode altitude. Enter an above home altitude in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:55
#: e64fce062a8540e49c56602dab290c30
msgid "A \"Guided\" target should appear on the map and the orange line (which indicates the target heading) should point to this guided target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:61
#: 9c95e9cc021a44908d0186cfaab35748
msgid "The vehicle should fly to the target location and wait there until you enter another location or switch to another mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:66
#: 5773b6e1d3b94dbbb9c6d1c716c6679c
msgid "On *Mission Planner* there is no need to set up one of your flight modes as \"Guided\". This may not be the case for other Ground Control Stations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:71
#: be1461dec3344606b30ba6285835c7b6
msgid "Speed Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:73
#: f843229aab24402394d1ef21a7e72f8a
msgid "The maximum horizontal speed of the copter can be adjusted with the **Speed** (:ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>`) parameter from the Mission Planner's Config/Tuning >> Copter Pids screen (see blue box above).  The default is 10 meaning 10m/s.  A typical copter can reach top speeds of 10m/s ~ 13m/s before it becomes unable to both maintain altitude and horizontal speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:80
#: 175f6afb06904437b9c5934da28e7dca
msgid "The vertical speeds up and down can similar be adjusted with the **Speed Up** (:ref:`WP_SPD_UP<WP_SPD_UP>`) and **Speed Dn** (:ref:`WP_SPD_DN<WP_SPD_DN>`) parameters. :ref:`WP_ACC_Z<WP_ACC_Z>` determines how fast the speed can change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:82
#: f2de52fa32d54cc691255e47239b3c61
msgid "Speed can also be controlled while in GUIDED mode with :ref:`MAVLink commands <common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd>` like :ref:`DO_CHANGE_SPEED<mav_cmd_do_change_speed>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:85
#: e91eca09f97e4ae3854da6f7b11768fa
msgid "Guided Mode Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:87
#: 7e1707d0b64f4448ad7df1a066a19d23
msgid "The :ref:`GUID_OPTIONS<GUID_OPTIONS>` parameter allows several guided mode behavior changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:90
#: 31c106b3c7c24252ad78fec61fa6b73f
msgid "Bit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:90
#: ae34f052776741bf9447b697bfa3419e
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:92
#: 1e52b4237a2d484ea470dc1258008a5f
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:92
#: fee2a2f16a73454a9461b337761f8a4d
msgid "Allow Arming from Transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:93
#: 7b2ad24b86134a9fb9671323c8bd5dd7
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:93
#: f7e6ab78ecf04822a39f16fc87fb5573
msgid "Ignore pilot yaw input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:94
#: 3e552f656a844bafba5d678ac524e306
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:94
#: 32fe8f18b7a64b9d9cadb2fd527c759b
msgid "SetAttitudeTarget interprets Thrust As Thrust"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:95
#: 68f77ceea9974a00b74dea72ecc16c88
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:95
#: d17c9c69bab644baadf6ec47e43646e0
msgid "Do not stabilize PositionXY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:96
#: 88bfc182b1c84ada8578d6a5a045fe1c
msgid "5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:96
#: ba8bce8e12264b059f07813afd4986c2
msgid "Do not stabilize VelocityXY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:97
#: a431cc2f8bc843df887fd0e83e643463
msgid "6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:97
#: 3e4ac281b18c4524afb6e44806ee51df
msgid "Waypoint navigation used for position targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:98
#: a564d9a1e69148ff97b3ef7460d970c7
msgid "7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:98
#: 7652c04e09e6492db258a2db70404e12
msgid "Allow weathervaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:101
#: 263cf65555214183bcf8ee6e58216ea1
msgid "Bit 0 (e.g. \"1\") allowing arming in Guided mode from the RC transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:103
#: 806f2ad2607442d7a26d4bc6463db4f2
msgid "Bit 2 (e.g. \"4\") disables the pilot's ability to change the vehicle's heading using the RC transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:105
#: b66dae37515a459fabb863cafb873bd3
msgid "Bit 3 (e.g. \"8\") changes the interpretation of the `SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET MAVLink <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET>`__ command's ``thrust`` field to be pure thrust expressed as a value between 0 and 1, instead of a climb rate. See :ref:`Copter Commands in Guided Mode <copter-commands-in-guided-mode>` for more details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:107
#: e76e2da60d504992ac3ed7882830199e
msgid "Bit 4 (e.g. \"16\") disables the position controller's XY axis position error correction.  This may be useful if an external controller is providing high speed targets which already include position error correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:109
#: 1abd004b41d94b5ea6810d8d978e04eb
msgid "Bit 5 (e.g. \"32\") is the same as above but affects the position controller's velocity error correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:111
#: cbaabe72b18b4cb3b7be7a7f58276f64
msgid "Bit 6 (e.g. \"64\") enables S-Curve path planning (the same as is used in :ref:`Auto mode <auto-mode>`) to reach the position target.  This may result a smoother acceleration and deceleration but the position target cannot be updated quickly.  This also allows :ref:`object avoidance path planning <common-object-avoidance-landing-page>` (e.g. :ref:`Bendy Ruler <common-oa-bendyruler>` and :ref:`Dijkstras<common-oa-dijkstras>`) to be used in Guided mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:113
#: 41ba0223c65248e081af91be007af3b4
msgid "Bit 7 (e.g. \"128\") enables :ref:`weathervaning <weathervaning>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:115
#: d1f251df303f4ed798d3f93f290661ab
msgid "The :ref:`GUID_TIMEOUT<GUID_TIMEOUT>` parameter holds the timeout (in seconds) when the vehicle is being controlled using attitude, velocity and/or acceleration commands. If no commands are received from the companion computer for this many seconds, the vehicle will slow to a stop (if velocity and/or acceleration commands were being provided) or hold a level hover (if attitude commands were provided). The default setting is 3 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:120
#: 10151299c8854fa1bd2dbb9ca5bf815d
msgid "Guided_NoGPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:121
#: f7194ec6a3054dd6abb71ee9ae3c8841
msgid "This variation of Guided mode does not require a GPS but it only accepts `attitude targets <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET>`__.  Because it does not accept position or velocity targets like regular Guided mode it is generally not useful for regular users.  This mode was created for use by companion computers that may want to fly the vehicle as if it was in AltHold mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_guidedmode.rst:125
#: d1f3b141905f4e34ac4ff437822cf1fd
msgid "Guided_NoGPS does not allow a vehicle to hold position without a GPS (i.e. non-GPS navigation).  For information on :ref:`non-GPS navigation see this wiki page <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page>`"
msgstr ""
